# Phase 13: Observability — P1-P2 (Metrics, Audit, Visualization)
# Status: NOT STARTED
# Depends on: Phase 11 (runtime integration for live data)
# Blocks: None

## Goal
Surface pipeline decisions as actionable metrics, audit trails, and
visualizations so operators can monitor cache health, debug regressions,
and optimize configurations without reading code.

## Why
- Pipeline makes ~20 decisions per turn (tier, budget, compaction, markers)
- Without observability, degradation is invisible until users complain
- Cache regressions cost money (miss = full recomputation = 10x latency)
- Operators need dashboards, not EXPLAIN output in logs

## Tasks

### 13.1 — Structured Metrics Emission
- [ ] Define metric names and labels:
  - `context_pipeline_pressure{tier,model}` — gauge
  - `context_pipeline_cache_hit_ratio{model,session_age}` — gauge
  - `context_pipeline_compact_events{strategy,tier}` — counter
  - `context_pipeline_phase_duration_us{phase}` — histogram
  - `context_pipeline_spill_bytes` — gauge
  - `context_pipeline_abort_count{reason}` — counter
  - `context_pipeline_shadow_diff_count` — counter (Phase 11 rollout)
- [ ] Emit via existing metrics infrastructure (Prometheus/OpenTelemetry)
- [ ] Per-session aggregation (avoid per-turn cardinality explosion)
- [ ] Unit test: metric emission for each decision path

### 13.2 — Audit Trail
- [ ] Store ContextAssemblyTrace per turn in session journal
- [ ] Include: tier selected, sections included/excluded, bytes cleared, markers placed
- [ ] Retention: keep last N turns per session (configurable, default: 20)
- [ ] Query API: GET /sessions/:id/context-traces (paginated)
- [ ] Schema: add context_traces table (session_id, turn_index, trace_json, created_at)

### 13.3 — Alert Rules
- [ ] Cache regression alert: hit ratio drops > 15% over 5 turns
- [ ] Pressure spike alert: raw pressure jumps > 0.20 in one turn
- [ ] Recovery loop alert: consecutive_ptl_errors >= 3
- [ ] Compaction cascade alert: 3+ compact events in 5 turns
- [ ] Cold cache alert: turn > 3 and ratio still == 0 (likely misconfiguration)
- [ ] Wire alerts to existing notification channels (log + optional webhook)

### 13.4 — EXPLAIN Mode for Users
- [ ] `/context explain` CLI command: show last turn's pipeline decisions
- [ ] Output: pressure, tier, sections (with token counts), cache markers, alerts
- [ ] Format: table (CLI) or JSON (API)
- [ ] Include recommendations when issues detected:
  - High pressure → "Consider reducing tool count or using schema pruning"
  - Cache cold → "Check if system prompt changed mid-session"
  - Recovery loop → "Tool may be producing unbounded output"

### 13.5 — Dashboard Visualization (admin UI)
- [ ] Session timeline: pressure + cache ratio over turns (line chart)
- [ ] Section budget breakdown per turn (stacked bar)
- [ ] Compaction events overlay (annotations on timeline)
- [ ] Model comparison: cache performance across models (table)
- [ ] Wire to existing Next.js admin dashboard (web/ directory)

## Acceptance Criteria
- All pipeline decisions emit at least one metric
- Audit trail queryable for any session within retention window
- Alert rules fire correctly for simulated degradation scenarios
- EXPLAIN output readable by operators without pipeline knowledge
- Dashboard renders for sessions with 50+ turns without lag

## Key Files
- astra-turn-core/src/context_assembly_trace.rs (trace data source)
- astra-turn-core/src/context_pipeline.rs (timing + decision points)
- runtime/src/server/ (API endpoints for trace query)
- web/ (Next.js admin dashboard)
- services/src/journals/ (audit trail storage)
